  "sourceFindings": [
    "The sole production changes reject an already-ended caller context before fleet launch and select caller cancellation while waiting for answers or the original hedge timer.",
    "Both changes invert exactly to the original full broker body; eight unchanged dependency bodies join the frozen base source map, and the new test path is absent.",
    "Original fleet ordering, answer choice, healthy and unusable answer policy, remembered peer, quota values, upload durability and retry policy are unchanged.",
    "Original len(peers)-buffered channel and exactly one send per launched peer allow late callback completion without requiring a coordinator receiver.",
    "Context cancellation returns the coordinator but cannot terminate an arbitrary callback. Deferred child-context cancellation and timer stop remain intact.",
    "Final tests observe callback entry, require the exact cancellation/deadline result before independent callback release, and join the test-owned coordinator in bounded cleanup.",
    "Callback-return observation is conditional on callback entry during early-failure cleanup, and does not instrument the private sender's final buffered-send instruction.",
    "The five-second real deadline allows a two-second callback-entry observation; the seven-second context observation and two-second cancellation-return bounds do not replace the real deadline.",
    "Ordinary Go select behavior retains no strict cancellation precedence when a usable answer and cancellation become ready together."
  ],
